# Copy this file to "contact.local" and put your contact on the first
# non-comment line. That file is git-ignored, so it never leaves your machine.
#
# The community API asks clients to identify themselves through the
# X-Super-Contact header, so its maintainers have a way to reach whoever is
# running a client that misbehaves. Anything reachable works:
#
#   you@example.com
#   github.com/your-handle
#   https://github.com/your-handle/your-repo
#
# HD2_API_CONTACT in the environment takes priority over this file. With
# neither set the tracker still runs and still sends the header, just with a
# placeholder instead of a way to reach you.
